<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sun Yat-sen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1866">1866</a>–<a href="/years/1925">1925</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sun Zhongshan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sun Yat-sen was a Chinese revolutionary and founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuomintang">Kuomintang</a> (Nationalist Party). After the 1911 revolution he became provisional president of the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> in January 1912 but soon gave way to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-shikai">Yuan Shikai</a>. He later led rival governments in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/beijing">Beijing</a> warlords, and his <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/three-principles-of-the-people">Three Principles of the People</a> made him the revered 'father of the nation' for both Nationalists and Communists.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sun-yat-sen.jpg" alt="Sun Yat-sen" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 上海波尔照相馆 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%AD%99%E4%B8%AD%E5%B1%B1%E8%82%96%E5%83%8F.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Republic of China grew out of the revolutionary movement against the Qing Empire led by <b>Sun Yat-sen</b>, whose Tongmenghui, or Revolutionary Alliance, was founded in Tokyo in 1905.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-china">Republic of China · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The Taiping mix of Christianity and radical social equality influenced <b>Sun Yat-sen</b>, and Chinese Communist historians, following Mao Zedong, called the rising proto-communist; John King Fairbank compared the Taiping with Mao’s communists.</blockquote><a href="/movement/taiping-rebellion">Taiping Rebellion · Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>The Constitution of the United States inspired constitution-makers well beyond those who copied its presidency, from Benito Juárez in Mexico to José Rizal in the Philippines and <b>Sun Yat-sen</b> in China, although since the 1980s new constitutions have more often looked elsewhere.</blockquote><a href="/government/presidential-democracy">Presidential democracy · Impact &amp; Legacy</a></li><li><blockquote>Japan’s defeat of Russia in 1905 awakened nationalism across Asia: in China <b>Sun Yat-sen</b> founded the Kuomintang, and the May Fourth Movement of 1919 followed.</blockquote><a href="/ideology/nationalism">Nationalism · Spread &amp; Variants</a></li><li><blockquote>It is often sung at funerals: those of <b>Sun Yat-sen</b> in 1925, of George V in 1936, of Queen Mary in 1953, of Jean, Grand Duke of Luxembourg, in 2019 and of Harald V of Norway in 2026.</blockquote><a href="/songs/abide-with-me">Abide with Me</a></li><li><blockquote>Its text was written jointly by four members of the Kuomintang, Hu Hanmin, Tai Chi-tao, Liao Zhongkai and Shao Yuanchong, and was first heard on 16 June 1924 as the opening of a speech by <b>Sun Yat-sen</b> at the opening ceremony of the Whampoa Military Academy.</blockquote><a href="/songs/three-principles-of-the-people">National Anthem of the Republic of China</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Cuiheng, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. Died in Peking Union Medical College Hospital, in what is now <a href="/countries/china">China</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=22.45,113.54&amp;year=1904" aria-label="Cuiheng on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7589 1335 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Sun Yat-sen"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M8039 1605h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M8039 1605h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=22.45,113.54&amp;year=1904">What was here in 1904? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
